<article class="env-lemma" id="0AQ6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AQ6">Lemma <span data-tag="0AQ6">87.24.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ and $g : Y \to Z$ be morphisms of formal algebraic spaces over $S$. If $g \circ f : X \to Z$ is locally of finite type, then $f : X \to Y$ is locally of finite type. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0AQ0" data-tag="0AQ0">87.19.3</a> we see that $f$ is representable by algebraic spaces. Let $T$ be a scheme and let $T \to Z$ be a morphism. Then we can apply Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0462" data-tag="0462">67.23.6</a> to the morphisms $T \times _ Z X \to T \times _ Z Y \to T$ of algebraic spaces to conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>